# ── Neovim runtime junk ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything below is machine-generated or machine-specific. The whole point of
# this repo is that a fresh clone + install script reproduces the setup, so none
# of it belongs in version control.

# Plugin code itself lives in stdpath("data"), not here, but be defensive in case
# someone ever vendors a plugin into the repo by accident.
nvim/lazy/
nvim/site/
nvim/spell/*.spl
nvim/spell/*.sug

# Session / shada / undo / swap, if any of them ever get pointed at the repo.
*.vim.session
*.shada
*.shada.tmp
*.un~
*.swp
*.swo

# ── Local-only overrides ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `lua/config/local.lua` is sourced at the very end of init.lua if it exists.
# Use it for machine-specific things you do NOT want on every box: a work proxy,
# a different font size, an extra LSP for a language only present on one machine.
nvim/lua/config/local.lua

# ── OS / editor cruft ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*~

# NOTE: lazy-lock.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It pins every plugin to an
# exact commit, which is what makes "clone on Linux" produce the same editor
# rather than whatever HEAD happens to be that day. Commit it.
